{"action": "amend", "added": [], "amendment": 1, "escalations": [], "frozen_at": "2026-09-03T23:19:36", "goals_canon": "f3e73e360652df75e86a404267563ff8786e47d3a3528bb6ce1fbe5572aebb28", "head": "76fad1b517f00134b2cca9db413de7dbfd5a7cbf", "modified": [{"new": "c1822a58afcd33cfd8110902e221c447f43f99b48d4d2ead046e1bc94c49b5c0", "old": "39840e782315f22d859d2287e586d4531d064378dd7df5c2345d17363a9b1503", "path": ".swarm-loop/acceptance/test_t2_resolver.py"}], "prev_frozen_at": "2026-09-03T21:20:49", "reason": "ESC-005 Option A, granted by the goal owner 2026-09-03. test_t2_resolver.py's sabotage companion for the namesake decoy flipped every 'no' verdict to 'yes' while KEEPING its contradicting evidence, and then required those documents to be ACCEPTED. That made a document explicitly naming a different employer AND a different city acceptable purely because the model attached 'yes' to it \u2014 contradicting DESIGN's 'negative evidence hard-rejects... a single contradiction must veto', which is a claim about the evidence rather than about which token the model emitted. It also could not distinguish 'polarity caused the rejection' from 'the contradiction caused it', because it moved the one dimension carrying both. AMENDED to flip the DISAMBIGUATOR instead: each decoy verdict becomes a 'yes' on 'role' carrying a different verbatim span from the same document, verified to assert no employer and no work location. Documents, confidences and source kinds are untouched, so the sabotage still proves the earlier rejection was not incidental. Verified: 14/14 t2 pass; and the amended test is NOT vacuous \u2014 a resolver sabotaged to drop those three doc ids from accepted_doc_ids makes it fail, with the sabotage confirmed present in the loaded source.", "removed": [], "seq": 3, "targets_moved": []}
